5,1,1,talk,Mizuki,,"To ensure we make a decision based on actual utility, I want to see the Post-occupancy review ratings and the Booking data for specialist and general rooms.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,Victoria,,I agree with Mizuki's focus on utility. I would like to look into the Timetable records on rooms out of service and the Booking data for specialist and general rooms as well.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,Benjamin,,"It seems we are prioritizing usage patterns. To complement that, I shall examine the Decade of delivery schedules by project rationale and the Survey findings in the older blocks. Logic suggests we check our track record.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,Kenji,,I want to know if the money we plan actually covers the work! I'll check the Tender records over three budget cycles and the Renewal reserve for equipment bought earlier.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Shunichi,,"Since we're discussing utility and budgets, we shouldn't forget the people. I'll look into the Staffing posts since the hiring freeze and the Bench technicians' weekly manual routines. Let's see who's actually doing the work.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,Mizuki,,"It seems we have a comprehensive spread of data. @Benjamin, @Kenji, and @Shunichi are covering the operational and financial risks, while Victoria and I focus on the user experience. I believe this balance is necessary.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""Kenji"",""Shunichi"",""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,Victoria,,"Indeed. By combining the usage data with the operational constraints others are investigating, we can avoid repeating past mistakes and ensure the chosen project is truly sustainable for the campus.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,Benjamin,,"A balanced approach is indeed the most rational one. I suspect we may find that our ambitions often clash with the reality of our infrastructure, but let us see what the data reveals.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,Kenji,,I'm just excited to see what's actually happening! I hope we find a way to make the budget work for everyone so we can get something awesome for the campus.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
14,1,2,talk,Shunichi,,"Let's hope your excitement is matched by some realistic numbers, Kenji. I'm more interested in whether we're just adding more tasks to an already exhausted staff. I'll be waiting for the results.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
15,1,3,talk,Mizuki,,"I think we have a solid plan. Since we have all our choices settled, I suggest we move forward to the data review phase to avoid any further delays.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
16,1,3,talk,Victoria,,"I agree. We have covered the financial, operational, and user-centric angles. There is no need for further deliberation until we have the facts in front of us.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
17,1,3,talk,Benjamin,,"Quite right. Efficiency is a virtue, and we have already partitioned the investigation logically. I am content to proceed and await the findings.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
18,1,3,talk,Kenji,,Me too! I'm ready to dive in and see what's going on with the money. Let's get to it!,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
19,1,3,talk,Shunichi,,I'm satisfied. We've divided the labor well enough. Let's get the data and see if the reality matches the rhetoric.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over.""}]}"
